                <pb facs="0157" n="125" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v06/pg125"/>

                <head>79. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>At the 371st meeting of the National Security Council on July 3, Allen W. Dulles
                    briefly commented on the situation in Cuba. According to the memorandum of
                    discussion, Dulles expressed his view that the news from Cuba was “a good deal
                    better, and that the Americans <pb facs="0158" n="126" xml:id="pg126"/> captured
                    by the rebel forces would be gradually freed in groups until all had been
                    released.” (Eisenhower Library, Whitman File, NSC Records)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
